# {{.Name}}

A [Warren](https://github.com/MerseniBilel/warren) service.

## Run it
{{- if eq .DB "postgres" }}

Migrate first. It is a DEPLOY STEP, run once before the new replicas start,
never a lifecycle hook — `cmd/migrate/main.go` says why in full.

```bash
export {{.EnvPrefix}}_DATABASE_URL='postgres://user:pass@localhost:5432/{{.Name}}?sslmode=disable'
go run ./cmd/migrate
```

Then:

```bash
{{.EnvPrefix}}_NAME={{.Name}} go run ./cmd/{{.Name}}
```

It boots the module graph, opens the pool, starts the outbox relay and the
notification consumer, opens readiness, and drains cleanly on SIGTERM.
Without `{{.EnvPrefix}}_NAME` or `{{.EnvPrefix}}_DATABASE_URL` it fails at
boot naming the variable — every error the framework can detect surfaces at
boot, never on request 1.
{{- else }}

```bash
